        "integrated_multimodal_description:\n[Shot 1] Generate only the missing interval between the protected end of the first excerpt and the protected beginning of the second excerpt from the same continuous soldier-crab shot. Preserve the real light-blue soldier crabs, low sand-level camera, cloudy sky, distant shoreline, natural color, shallow depth of field, and documentary motion. Continue every visible crab from its incoming direction and gait. During the missing interval, the foreground group advances laterally across the damp sand while several crabs pass behind it at different depths. Keep the camera's existing low position and gentle drift physically continuous, avoid any cut, speed ramp, freeze, duplicated animal, or sudden composition change, and converge early enough that positions, focus, camera motion, lighting, and crab gait settle exactly into the protected second endpoint.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nContinue the same location recording through the missing interval: coastal wind, distant surf, faint water movement, and quiet crab-leg scratches. Match level, spatial character, and timing at both protected audio endpoints without adding speech or a discontinuity.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
